  <!-- Mouse drag readers for sliders, range controls and scroll bars. Each is
       spoken only while the mouse is actually dragging the control, and only
       when the announced number changes.
       SliderLabelledValue joins a slider's name to its value ({0} = the name,
       {1} = the value), and is used once at the start of a drag, for a name
       that was drawn as a name and value pair on the previous pass: the name
       is still right but its number is one pass old, so the live one is
       spoken beside it. Every other slider drag opens with the name alone and
       then speaks values on their own, so nothing ever doubles up.
       RangeMinimum / RangeMaximum name the thumb a drag is moving on a
       two-handle range control; {0} is that thumb's value in the control's own
       rendering.
       ScrollPercent / ScrollPercentAcross report how far a scroll bar has been
       dragged, down and across respectively, as a share of the scrollable
       extent. -->
